{"candidates":[{"content":"The isolated artifact abstracts the foundation's specific mean-principle derivation into a general covering principle: for any constraint pair (sum S, structure 'three consecutive even integers'), the solution is the unique triple satisfying both constraints simultaneously. It abstracts SRC_012's empiric-style verification and SRC_010's mean derivation into a single satisficing framework. This abstraction is refuted if the foundation's concrete derivation cannot be recovered by instantiating S=138 and structure=consecutive-even, or if some other triple also satisfies both constraints simultaneously (which would destroy uniqueness and hence the covering claim).","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"0b13382ebfe26920ba6277cd143fa58aafb46add4f90c8a95a75f0a0bdb4bc55"},{"role":"dependence","target":"312e145209d1b2bf8783c4789f786720136b7c5da8accf82a61e0829f09e2752"},{"role":"dependence","target":"3ac04247fac45e1175913e52e7146aa68d47b7843a6246e460100754b72de59c"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672"},{"role":"dependence","target":"2316baad7b12326eaa49a37bacb6e6b07c11b9fe82018e24c78fe7496ed5397a"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ca650e7eb41f9a77dc2cdd79606d2246ec9b8e8bf62882d0876857bd14650048"}],"typicality":0.65},{"content":"The isolated artifact contradicts the foundation by rejecting the mean principle as the operative causal mechanism. Where SRC_010 and SRC_008 derive the answer by computing 138/3=46 as the middle term, the isolated artifact instead activates a parity-exclusion mechanism: it first tests consecutive integers (45,46,47) and rejects them for failing the even constraint, arriving at 44,46,48 not by mean inversion but by counterexample-driven constraint pruning. The mean principle is an incidental descriptive coincidence, not the generative cause. This contradiction is refuted if the parity-exclusion route fails to independently determine the triple without appealing to the mean value 46 as input.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"93a5c498dbc5fc074c84c4a3ae4dfa42aa8e5d2b0eab0b9294e9c821218eb975"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ca650e7eb41f9a77dc2cdd79606d2246ec9b8e8bf62882d0876857bd14650048"},{"role":"dependence","target":"20acccc2034086f53bc6d59aac43d5efe56b90a29e42513f212996ab88dbce5f"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ba687c5f145e404c53a84549cf366e0b6e0106eec67404c07231357fed09e672"},{"role":"dependence","target":"e7bb307edea5a70dc2260902793322c5be8265d5da5cfaac6d8073053a463e0d"}],"typicality":0.25},{"content":"The isolated artifact reduces to SRC_011's arithmetic-progression formalization: the problem reduces to solving 3a+6=138 for the least term, yielding a=44 and largest a+4=48. All other foundation artifacts (mean principle in SRC_010, parity offset in SRC_008, verification in SRC_012) are subsumed as special cases of the AP formula Sum = n/2 * (first + last). This reduction is refuted if the AP formalization produces a different answer for S=138 with common difference 2, or if it cannot derive the mean principle as a corollary.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"cffd3373074eb70c8f0002c0b7978aea57c98169dce1159ff3de374cf308a2dc"},{"role":"dependence","target":"312e145209d1b2bf8783c4789f786720136b7c5da8accf82a61e0829f09e2752"},{"role":"dependence","target":"3ac04247fac45e1175913e52e7146aa68d47b7843a6246e460100754b72de59c"},{"role":"dependence","target":"2316baad7b12326eaa49a37bacb6e6b07c11b9fe82018e24c78fe7496ed5397a"},{"role":"dependence","target":"260e80545065ca2d607491f7a50dfd5215c9a25786e5d3a31202757db157b877"}],"typicality":0.7},{"content":"The isolated artifact shares mechanism with SRC_008's offset-class inference but extends it: SRC_008 checks divisibility by 3 to confirm an even center exists, then directly produces the triple. The shared mechanism is parity-gated mean inversion — the sum must split into a middle term whose parity matches the required offset class. The isolated artifact integrates this with SRC_009's counterexample rejection by showing that the parity gate simultaneously excludes (45,46,47) and necessitates (44,46,48) through one mechanism rather than two. This shared-mechanism claim is refuted if the parity gate operates independently from the mean inversion step, i.e., if the triple could be found by parity reasoning alone without ever determining the mean 46.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"3ac04247fac45e1175913e52e7146aa68d47b7843a6246e460100754b72de59c"},{"role":"dependence","target":"93a5c498dbc5fc074c84c4a3ae4dfa42aa8e5d2b0eab0b9294e9c821218eb975"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ca650e7eb41f9a77dc2cdd79606d2246ec9b8e8bf62882d0876857bd14650048"},{"role":"dependence","target":"b03c164328561538ee0e59e2ac7fb421e01732d1f8f46a5a31720980ea0f5719"},{"role":"dependence","target":"20acccc2034086f53bc6d59aac43d5efe56b90a29e42513f212996ab88dbce5f"}],"typicality":0.5},{"content":"The isolated artifact inherits from SRC_012's verification-first methodology: SRC_012 confirms 44+46+48=138 as a reconstruction step after proposing the triple. The isolated artifact generalizes this into a constructive-then-verificative protocol that applies to any Diophantine constraint system — propose via structure, verify via both constraints simultaneously. The inheritance is refuted if SRC_012's verification step can be removed without loss of correctness (making verification an inert ceremony rather than an inherited obligation), or if the isolated artifact's protocol fails on the canonical instance S=138, structure=three-consecutive-even.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"0b13382ebfe26920ba6277cd143fa58aafb46add4f90c8a95a75f0a0bdb4bc55"},{"role":"dependence","target":"312e145209d1b2bf8783c4789f786720136b7c5da8accf82a61e0829f09e2752"},{"role":"dependence","target":"e7bb307edea5a70dc2260902793322c5be8265d5da5cfaac6d8073053a463e0d"},{"role":"dependence","target":"ba687c5f